    <p>The distribution of month-over-month changes is notably <strong>leptokurtic</strong> (fat-tailed) with a skewness of {mom_data.skew():.2f} and excess kurtosis of {mom_data.kurtosis():.2f}, indicating that extreme moves occur far more frequently than a normal distribution would predict. This has critical implications for risk management — Value-at-Risk models based on normal assumptions systematically underestimate tail risk in oil markets.</p>

