    <p>The interquartile range of <strong>${price_p75 - price_p25:.2f}</strong> (from ${price_p25:.2f} to ${price_p75:.2f}) captures the "typical" price environment, while the full range of ${overall_range:.2f} demonstrates how extreme events create observations far outside the central tendency. The excess kurtosis of <strong>{price_kurt:.2f}</strong> confirms the leptokurtic nature of the distribution — heavy tails relative to a normal distribution.</p>

